Copyright (c) 2026 Proximi.io. All rights reserved.


1. WHAT THIS DOCUMENT COVERS

1.1  "Map" means the precompiled Proximi.io iOS map package distributed from
     this repository: the `ProximiioMapBinary.xcframework` attached to each
     release, the package manifest, the one-line source shim, and the
     accompanying documentation. It does not mean the map's source code, which
     is not published.

1.2  The Map is not self-contained. Adding it to a build also brings in the
     Proximi.io iOS SDK and the MapLibre renderer, each at the exact version
     this release was compiled against. The SDK is Proximi.io software under
     its own copy of this licence (clause 6.3); MapLibre is third-party
     software under its own licence (clause 8.1).

1.3  "You" means the legal entity exercising the rights below, and every entity
     that entity controls.

1.4  The Map is licensed, not sold. Proximi.io grants you the rights in
     clause 2 and keeps everything else.


2. LICENCE GRANT

Subject to clauses 3, 7 and 11, Proximi.io grants you a non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable, worldwide licence, for the term described
in clause 11, to:

2.1  download, install and store copies of the Map;

2.2  integrate the Map into applications you develop ("your Applications") and
     make copies of it as your build process requires;

2.3  distribute the Map, in its compiled form, embedded inside your
     Applications — through the Apple App Store, TestFlight, Apple Business
     Manager, an enterprise distribution programme, or any equivalent channel —
     to end users of those Applications; and

2.4  use the Map internally for development, testing and support of your
     Applications.

2.5  No licence to end users. Your end users receive the Map only as an
     inseparable part of your Application. They get no rights in the Map of
     their own, and your Application's own end-user terms must not purport to
     grant them any.


3. WHAT THE LICENCE DOES NOT ALLOW

Except where a mandatory law gives you a right that cannot be contracted away
(and then only to the extent of that right), you must not, and must not permit
anyone else to:

3.1  reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise attempt to derive
     the source code, algorithms or internal design of the Map, whether by
     static analysis of the binary, instrumentation of it at runtime, or any
     other means;

3.2  extract, isolate, re-link or repackage any part of the Map so that it can
     be used outside one of your Applications — including lifting the
     xcframework, or any object code, symbol or resource out of it, into
     another library, framework, package, container or service;

3.3  distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent, lease, lend or otherwise make
     the Map available as a library, SDK, package, component or hosted service,
     whether on its own or bundled with other software. Clause 2.3 is the only
     redistribution this licence permits: inside your Application, as part of
     its compiled product;

3.4  use the Map, or anything you learn from it, to build, train, improve or
     operate a product that competes with the Map, the Proximi.io iOS SDK, or
     the Proximi.io platform — including an indoor positioning, indoor
     wayfinding, or venue mapping SDK or service;

3.5  remove, obscure or alter any copyright notice, licence text, attribution,
     product identifier or code signature in the Map or in the third-party
     components it brings with it. This includes the on-map attribution control
     described in clause 8.3;

3.6  circumvent or disable any licence check, token validation, quota or usage
     measurement in the Map or in the Proximi.io services it talks to, or use
     the Map with credentials you are not entitled to use; or

3.7  represent the Map, or the venue rendering it produces, as your own
     technology in a way that misstates its origin.

3.8  Clause 3 restricts the Proximi.io portions of this distribution only. It
     does not restrict anything MapLibre's own licence permits you to do with
     MapLibre (clause 8.1).


4. THE PUBLIC REPOSITORY IS NOT A PUBLIC LICENCE

4.1  This repository is public so that Swift Package Manager can resolve it
     without credentials. That is a mechanical necessity of how Swift Package
     Manager fetches packages, not an offer of open-source terms.

4.2  Being able to read the repository, clone it, or download a release asset
     gives you no licence to use the Map. The rights in clause 2 exist only
     while you hold a valid Proximi.io commercial agreement (clause 7). Absent
     that agreement, any use beyond evaluating whether to enter into one is
     unlicensed.

4.3  The Map is not open source, and nothing about the repository's visibility
     makes it so. No open-source licence — permissive or copyleft — applies to
     the Proximi.io portions of this distribution. MapLibre, which does carry
     an open-source licence, is a component this package depends on; its
     licence applies to it and not to the Map. Do not read MapLibre's BSD
     licence as covering anything in `ProximiioMapBinary.xcframework`.


5. OWNERSHIP

5.1  Proximi.io and its licensors own the Map and every intellectual property
     right in it, including the rendering, styling and route-drawing methods it
     implements. Nothing in this licence transfers any of that to you.

5.2  You own your Applications and everything you write. Integrating the Map
     gives Proximi.io no rights in your code.

5.3  This licence grants no trademark rights. You may state factually that your
     Application uses Proximi.io technology; any other use of Proximi.io's
     names or logos needs written permission. MapLibre's and MapTiler's marks
     are theirs, not Proximi.io's to license.

5.4  If you send Proximi.io feedback, bug reports or suggestions, Proximi.io may
     use them without obligation to you. This does not give Proximi.io any
     licence to your Applications or to your data.


6. THE MAP NEEDS A PROXIMI.IO ACCOUNT, AND IT NEEDS THE SDK

6.1  The Map does nothing useful on its own. It requires a Proximi.io account
     and a valid token, and it works against Proximi.io services whose terms,
     availability and pricing are set in your commercial agreement, not here.

6.2  This licence does not entitle you to those services, to any service level,
     to support, or to any future release of the Map. Those come from the
     commercial agreement, if it provides them.

6.3  The Proximi.io iOS SDK arrives with the Map and is licensed to you under
     the licence shipped with the SDK's own distribution, not under this file.
     The two texts are written to say the same thing, but if they ever differ,
     the SDK's licence governs the SDK and this one governs the Map.


7. RELATIONSHIP TO YOUR COMMERCIAL AGREEMENT

7.1  This file states the terms on which the binary Map may be used. Your
     separate written commercial agreement with Proximi.io — subscription
     agreement, master services agreement, order form, or equivalent — states
     the commercial relationship: fees, term, service levels, data processing,
     support, and the like.

7.2  Where the two conflict, the commercial agreement prevails, and this file
     is read as narrowed or widened to match it. If your commercial agreement
     grants you rights this file does not, you have those rights. If it imposes
     restrictions this file does not, those restrictions apply.

7.3  If you have no commercial agreement with Proximi.io, this file governs on
     its own, and clause 4.2 applies: you have no licence to use the Map in
     production.

7.4  This file is not an entire-agreement clause and does not replace anything
     you have already signed.


8. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Map brings third-party software with it. Those components are licensed to
you by their own licensors under their own terms, not by Proximi.io under this
licence. Clause 9's disclaimer and clause 10's liability limits apply to them
as they reach you through the Map.

The full notices are in the two files published beside this one:
`ThirdParty-MapLibre-LICENSE.txt` and `NOTICES.md`. Both must travel with any
Application that ships this package. This clause summarises what they require;
they are the operative text.

8.1  MapLibre Native — BSD 2-Clause licence.

     Version: the one pinned `exact:` in this release's `Package.swift`
     (6.29.0 at the time this draft was written).
     Copyright (c) 2021 MapLibre contributors; (c) 2018-2021 MapTiler.com;
     (c) 2014-2020 Mapbox.

     MapLibre is not compiled into `ProximiioMapBinary.xcframework`. Your
     package manager resolves it as a separate binary target, and your build
     embeds and signs `MapLibre.framework` into your Application. Your
     Application therefore distributes MapLibre in binary form.

     What you must do: the BSD 2-Clause licence requires that a binary
     redistribution reproduce MapLibre's copyright notice, the list of
     conditions, and the disclaimer "in the documentation and/or other
     materials provided with the distribution". In an iOS app that means a
     legal, licences or acknowledgements screen, or equivalent in-app or
     accompanying documentation. Reproduce the full text of
     `ThirdParty-MapLibre-LICENSE.txt` there. Shipping without it is a licence
     violation by your Application, and Proximi.io cannot cure it for you — we
     can only hand you the text.

     The Mapbox copyright line is part of the required notice: MapLibre Native
     descends from Mapbox GL Native as it stood before Mapbox's licence change.

8.2  The Proximi.io iOS SDK, and GRDB.swift through it — MIT licence.

     The SDK is Proximi.io software (clause 6.3) and carries no separate
     third-party obligation of its own, but it embeds GRDB.swift
     (github.com/groue/GRDB.swift), which is MIT-licensed, © 2015-2025 Gwendal
     Roué. Every Application that ships this package also ships GRDB. The MIT
     licence requires its copyright notice and permission notice to be included
     with every copy; the full text is in `NOTICES.md` and in the SDK's own
     licence file. Put it on the same screen as the MapLibre notice.

8.3  On-map attribution is a separate obligation, and it is not the same one.

     The Map shows MapLibre's attribution control (the ⓘ) by default, and
     `MapCanvasConfiguration` lets you move, tint and re-label it. Leave it
     visible.

     That control attributes the map *data* — OpenStreetMap and whichever tile
     or style provider your venue uses — and satisfies those providers' terms.
     It does not satisfy MapLibre's software licence, which asks for the
     copyright notice, conditions and disclaimer in your documentation or
     accompanying materials, not a link in the corner of a view. You need both:
     the attribution control and the notice screen in clause 8.1.

     Map data and tile terms are between you and whoever serves your tiles.
     Proximi.io does not license OpenStreetMap data to you.

8.4  SQLite — no obligation on you.

     The Map links SQLite through Apple's system library,
     `/usr/lib/libsqlite3.dylib`. Proximi.io does not distribute SQLite to you;
     Apple does, as part of iOS. Your use of it is covered by your Apple
     developer agreements. SQLite itself is in the public domain and asks for
     no attribution.

8.5  Nothing else ships. Apart from MapLibre, the SDK and GRDB above, the Map
     binary declares no dynamic dependency other than the Apple system
     frameworks and `libsqlite3.dylib`, and embeds no other third-party code.

8.6  If a future release changes this list, `NOTICES.md` shipped with that
     release states the change. Check the files that came with the version you
     ship — in particular the MapLibre version, which is pinned exactly and
     moves between releases.


9. NO WARRANTY

9.1  THE MAP IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY
     KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE IMPLIED
     WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE AND
     NON-INFRINGEMENT.

9.2  Proximi.io does not warrant that the Map will be uninterrupted or
     error-free, or that any position, floor, geofence event, route or rendered
     geometry it presents will be accurate. Indoor positioning is an estimate
     derived from radio and inertial signals, and venue geometry is only as
     current as the data published for that venue — things that depend on the
     venue, the hardware, the installation and the environment, and are outside
     Proximi.io's control.

9.3  You must not use the Map as the sole means of determining position or of
     guiding a person where an error could cause death, personal injury, or
     serious physical or environmental damage. It is not designed, tested or
     certified for navigation of vehicles or aircraft, for medical use, for
     emergency egress or emergency response dispatch, or for any other
     safety-critical purpose.

9.4  Clause 9 is capitalised because several jurisdictions require a warranty
     disclaimer to be conspicuous for it to take effect. It does not exclude a
     warranty that a mandatory consumer or commercial law gives you and does
     not permit to be excluded.


10. LIABILITY

10.1 Proximi.io is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential
     or punitive damages, nor for lost profits, lost revenue, lost data, or
     business interruption, arising out of or relating to the Map, however
     caused and on any theory of liability, even if Proximi.io has been advised
     that such damage is possible.

10.2 Proximi.io's total aggregate liability arising out of or relating to the
     Map and this licence is capped at the amount you paid Proximi.io under
     your commercial agreement in the twelve months before the event giving
     rise to the claim. [CAP — TO BE CONFIRMED: see Open decisions, item 3.]

10.3 Nothing in this licence excludes or limits liability that cannot lawfully
     be excluded or limited, including liability for death or personal injury
     caused by negligence, and for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation.

10.4 You are responsible for your Applications: for what they do with the
     positions and geometry the Map presents, for the permissions they ask of
     their users, for surfacing the third-party notices in clause 8, and for
     their compliance with applicable law, Apple's App Store rules, and data
     protection law. You will defend and indemnify Proximi.io against
     third-party claims arising from your Applications, except to the extent
     the claim is caused by the Map itself.


11. TERM AND TERMINATION

11.1 This licence starts when you first download or use the Map and runs for as
     long as your commercial agreement with Proximi.io is in force.

11.2 It terminates automatically if your commercial agreement terminates or
     expires. Proximi.io may also terminate it on written notice if you breach
     clause 3 or clause 4 and, where the breach can be cured, do not cure it
     within 30 days of notice.

11.3 On termination you must stop using the Map in development, stop shipping
     new versions of your Applications that contain it, and delete the copies
     you hold. Proximi.io will not require you to recall or remotely disable
     copies already installed on end users' devices; those copies may remain in
     place, and clauses 3, 5, 8, 9, 10 and 12 keep applying to them.
     Termination of this licence does not terminate your MapLibre rights, which
     come from MapLibre's own licence and are not Proximi.io's to withdraw.

11.4 Clauses 3, 4.2, 5, 8, 9, 10, 11.3 and 12 survive termination.


12. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTES

12.1 This licence is governed by the laws of [GOVERNING LAW — TO BE DECIDED,
     see Open decisions, item 2], excluding its conflict-of-law rules and
     excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of
     Goods.

12.2 The courts of [FORUM — TO BE DECIDED, see Open decisions, item 2] have
     exclusive jurisdiction, except that either party may seek injunctive
     relief for infringement of intellectual property rights in any competent
     court.

12.3 If your commercial agreement names a governing law or forum, that one
     applies instead, per clause 7.2.


13. GENERAL

13.1 You may not assign this licence without Proximi.io's written consent,
     except to a successor of your whole business, on written notice.

13.2 If a clause is held unenforceable, it is narrowed to the minimum extent
     that makes it enforceable, or struck if it cannot be; the rest stands.

13.3 A delay in enforcing a term is not a waiver of it.

13.4 Proximi.io may publish revised licence terms with a future release. The
     terms shipped in the release you use govern that release; they do not
     change retroactively for releases you already shipped.

13.5 Questions about this licence: support@proximi.io.


